  "helpMoneyStep1Title": "Pick a month",
  "helpMoneyStep1Body": "Use the arrows at the top to see another month.",
  "helpMoneyStep2Title": "Spent and pace",
  "helpMoneyStep2Body": "What you’ve spent so far, and where you’ll be by the month’s end at this pace.",
  "helpMoneyStep3Title": "Where it went",
  "helpMoneyStep3Body": "Spending by category, biggest first.",
  "helpMoneyStep4Title": "Cash flow",
  "helpMoneyStep4Body": "Money in, money out and what’s left over. Moves between your own accounts don’t count.",
  "helpMoneyStep5Title": "Worth a look",
  "helpMoneyStep5Body": "Notes on budgets and entries to categorize, when there’s something to see.",
  "helpNewTransactionSummary": "Record money spent, earned or moved between your accounts.",
  "helpNewTransactionStep1Title": "Pick the kind",
  "helpNewTransactionStep1Body": "Spend, Income or Transfer. The amount and date stay when you switch.",
  "helpNewTransactionStep2Title": "Say it",
  "helpNewTransactionStep2Body": "Tap the mic and say, for example, “Spent 45 at Panda with Visa yesterday”. Qima fills in the form on this device; check it and tap Save.",
  "helpNewTransactionStep3Title": "Category",
  "helpNewTransactionStep3Body": "Spending and income go in a category. A move between your own accounts is never spending.",
  "helpNewTransactionStep4Title": "Declined",
  "helpNewTransactionStep4Body": "Turn on Declined for a payment that didn’t go through: it’s shown struck through and never counts.",
  "helpTransactionsSummary": "Every transaction, newest first, and what each one did to your accounts.",
  "helpTransactionsStep1Title": "Open one",
  "helpTransactionsStep1Body": "Tap a transaction to see each account it touched, and by how much.",
  "helpTransactionsStep2Title": "How it counts",
  "helpTransactionsStep2Body": "Each one says whether it’s spending, income, a move between your accounts or a change in value.",
  "helpTransactionsStep3Title": "Edit or delete",
  "helpTransactionsStep3Body": "Open it, then edit or delete it. Deleting puts every account back as it was.",
  "helpAccountsSummary": "Bank accounts, cash, cards and loans, with what’s in each one today.",
  "helpAccountsStep1Title": "Add an account",
  "helpAccountsStep1Body": "Give it a name, a type and its balance today. Qima starts from that figure.",
  "helpAccountsStep2Title": "Check the balance",
  "helpAccountsStep2Body": "Open an account and enter what your bank shows. For a difference, choose: add a transaction for it, or change the opening balance so nothing counts as spending.",
  "helpAccountsStep3Title": "Count cash",
  "helpAccountsStep3Body": "For cash, count what’s in your wallet and Qima sets the balance to it.",
  "helpAccountsStep4Title": "Pay a card or loan",
  "helpAccountsStep4Body": "Open the card or loan and tap Pay to record a payment from another account.",
  "helpAccountsStep5Title": "Remove one",
  "helpAccountsStep5Body": "An account with transactions is archived so its history still adds up. One never used is deleted.",
  "helpBalanceSheetSummary": "Everything you own and everything you owe, adding up to your net worth.",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep1Title": "What you own",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep1Body": "Accounts, holdings at live prices, and assets at the value you set.",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep2Title": "What you owe",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep2Body": "Cards, loans (principal only) and money you owe people.",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep3Title": "How the total is worked out",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep3Body": "Open it to see each rule, such as the live rate used for other currencies.",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep4Title": "Leave one out",
  "helpBalanceSheetStep4Body": "Turn off Count in net worth on an account or asset; its history still adds up.",
  "helpAssetsSummary": "A home, land, a car or a share in a business, at the value you set.",
  "helpAssetsStep1Title": "Add an asset",
  "helpAssetsStep1Body": "Pick a kind, then give it a value and a date. Gold and silver by weight are holdings instead.",
  "helpAssetsStep2Title": "Update the value",
  "helpAssetsStep2Body": "Every update is dated. The latest counts; older values stay as history.",
  "helpAssetsStep3Title": "A loan on it",
  "helpAssetsStep3Body": "Link the loan secured on it to see what’s still owed next to its value.",
  "helpAssetsStep4Title": "Sold it",
  "helpAssetsStep4Body": "Record the sale: the money goes into an account and the asset leaves your balance sheet.",
  "helpImportStatementSummary": "Bring in transactions from your bank’s PDF, Excel or CSV, screenshots, or a copied file.",
  "helpImportStatementStep1Title": "Pick the files",
  "helpImportStatementStep1Body": "From Files, Photos, the clipboard, or Share › Qima from any app. They’re read on this device.",
  "helpImportStatementStep2Title": "Check every row",
  "helpImportStatementStep2Body": "Pick the account, untick what you don’t want and fix any category. Rows already in Qima start unticked.",
  "helpImportStatementStep3Title": "Match the balance",
  "helpImportStatementStep3Body": "When the statement shows a balance, tick Bring the balance to it. Then choose how: change the opening balance, or add a transaction for the difference.",
  "helpImportStatementStep4Title": "Add them",
  "helpImportStatementStep4Body": "Tap Add. The files are deleted once imported.",
  "helpBankMessagesSummary": "Add purchases from the messages your bank sends you, after you check each one.",
  "helpBankMessagesStep1Title": "On Android",
  "helpBankMessagesStep1Body": "Turn on Read new bank messages and allow access. Bring in the last 60 days the first time.",
  "helpBankMessagesStep2Title": "On iPhone",
  "helpBankMessagesStep2Body": "Set up a Shortcuts automation once, so each bank message goes to Qima’s Add a bank message action.",
  "helpBankMessagesStep3Title": "Check before adding",
  "helpBankMessagesStep3Body": "Messages wait in the import review. Codes, offers and repeats are skipped.",
  "helpBankMessagesStep4Title": "Private",
  "helpBankMessagesStep4Body": "Messages are read on this device and never leave it.",
  "helpCategoriesSummary": "Sort spending into categories, and teach Qima where each name goes.",
  "helpCategoriesStep1Title": "To categorize",
  "helpCategoriesStep1Body": "Pick a category once for each name. Imports from that name use it from now on.",
  "helpCategoriesStep2Title": "Earlier entries",
  "helpCategoriesStep2Body": "Qima offers to move earlier entries from the same name too.",
  "helpCategoriesStep3Title": "Your categories",
  "helpCategoriesStep3Body": "Add, rename or remove categories. Transactions in a removed one keep it in their history.",
  "helpCategoriesStep4Title": "Forget a name",
  "helpCategoriesStep4Body": "Forget what Qima learned for a name, and its imports are sorted by hand again.",
  "helpBudgetSummary": "A monthly amount for each category you want to watch.",
  "helpBudgetStep1Title": "Set an amount",
  "helpBudgetStep1Body": "Tap a category and enter its amount per month. Zero removes it.",
  "helpBudgetStep2Title": "Left to spend",
  "helpBudgetStep2Body": "Home shows what’s left this month, and Money notes a category that’s ahead of its pace.",
  "helpBudgetStep3Title": "What counts",
  "helpBudgetStep3Body": "Card payments, transfers and loan principal never count.",
  "helpRecurringSummary": "Rent, bills and subscriptions, shown in Coming up before they’re due.",
  "helpRecurringStep1Title": "Add one",
  "helpRecurringStep1Body": "Give it a name, an amount, the account it’s paid from and its day of the month.",
  "helpRecurringStep2Title": "Coming up",
  "helpRecurringStep2Body": "Home lists the next ones due, so nothing takes you by surprise.",
  "helpRecurringStep3Title": "Change or remove",
  "helpRecurringStep3Body": "Tap one to change it or remove it.",
  "helpPeopleSummary": "Who owes you, whom you owe, and the repayments.",
  "helpPeopleStep1Title": "Lent or borrowed",
  "helpPeopleStep1Body": "Tap + › More › Lent or Borrowed, and type the person’s name.",
  "helpPeopleStep2Title": "Repayments",
  "helpPeopleStep2Body": "Record Repayment received or Repayment made, and what’s owed goes down.",
  "helpPeopleStep3Title": "Bill split",
  "helpPeopleStep3Body": "Pay a whole bill and split it: only your share is spending, the rest is owed to you.",
  "helpFeaturesSummary": "Turn parts of Qima on or off. Features also turn on by themselves the first time you use them.",
  "helpFeaturesStep1Title": "Turn one off",
  "helpFeaturesStep1Body": "Its screens hide, never your money: its amounts still count on the balance sheet.",
